<h2 id="draft-collections">Keep several articles in a private collection</h2>
<p>In the public writer or any converter, open Keep several articles in a private collection above the editor. Add current writing as a new saved article captures its full workspace, including source notes, audience, purpose, page fields, and private review questions. The article can be incomplete. Use a saved article name to identify it; that name does not change its article title.</p>
<p>Editing the current article does not update a saved entry. Select an entry and use Update selected from current writing when you want that snapshot to keep the current edits. Use Rename selected article to change only its collection label. Inspect the selected private workspace shows the exact saved source and article in a read-only JSON field. Closing inspection clears its hidden text.</p>
<p>Open selected article replaces the editor only after confirmation when it contains different writing. A valid current workspace is kept in Revisions before replacement; invalid current fields or unavailable checkpoint protection block opening. Opening clears approval and the publishing profile, including checklist ticks. The collection itself is unchanged. Article imports, workspace restore, and checkpoint restore change the editor while keeping the collection.</p>
<p>Undo last collection change recovers one add, update, rename, removal, or collection load. It changes only saved entries, never the current editor. A further collection change replaces that undo state. Clear this writing desk removes the article, notes, profile, collection, collection undo, and all checkpoints from this tab after confirmation. Downloaded files are unchanged.</p>
<ol><li>Save the articles you need with Add or Update. Each collection holds up to eight saved workspaces, within a 2 MiB JSON-file limit. Entries are never automatically evicted to make room.</li><li>Acknowledge that the file contains every saved article and its private source and review notes. Download private draft collection, then check the actual file before leaving. Only saved entries are included; current edits need an explicit Add or Update first.</li><li>On your next visit, choose Load a private collection to preview. Inspect its entry names and sizes, then choose Load this collection. Loading replaces only saved entries, keeps editor writing and approval unchanged, and supports one-step undo. Cancel preview changes nothing.</li><li>Select and open a saved article separately. Review it again before copying or exporting. The app makes no upload or publishing request.</li></ol>
<p>Collections are unencrypted private files. Keep them out of public repositories and inspect them before sharing. They exclude sign-in fields, approval, publishing profiles, temporary checks, pending imports, checkpoints, and collection undo. A collection is separate from a single-workspace backup and from an article publishing kit. Article exports still contain only the current article. Neither collection entries nor edits are saved automatically in browser or server storage. Refreshing or leaving can discard everything that was not explicitly downloaded.</p>
